# G089 — Transaction Averages

*v2. See `transaction-averages.md` for prose: group-by as single-pass
fold, observation and finalisation as explicit steps, integer cents
throughout, output sorted by key for determinism, key function over
key field.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Vault Finance Ledger

[vault-finance-ledger @ledger-path
    IN ORDER TO
        ingest a CSV ledger, aggregate along several axes at once
        render a summary card, and support category drill-down
        without re-reading the file between views

    @text <- [vault[read-string {path: @ledger-path}]]
    @txns <- [ta[parse {text: @text}]]

    [ui[render-summary
          {total:       [ta[total        {txns: @txns}]],
           by-category: [ta[by-category  {txns: @txns}]],
           by-month:    [ta[by-month     {txns: @txns}]]}]]

    sync @user-events {
        pick-category @cat ->
            @filtered <- @txns where category is @cat
            [ui[render-detail
                  {txns: @filtered,
                   stats: [ta[total {txns: @filtered}]]}]]
    }
]

---

## Verb Surface

[ta
    parse-transaction   {line}                    ;; -> Transaction | none
    parse               {text}                     ;; -> [Transaction]
    group-by            {txns, key-fn}             ;; -> [(String, Stats)]
    by-category         {txns}
    by-month            {txns}
    total               {txns}                      ;; -> Stats
    top-n-by-mean       {groups, n}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: observe and finalise as `where` phases

[ta[group-by {txns: @txns, key-fn: @keys}]
    IN ORDER TO
        pass over @txns once updating per-key running state
        then finalise each accumulator into means
        and emit groups ordered by key so output is deterministic

    @txns
        gathered by @keys into @accumulators
        where each observation updates count, sum-cents, min-cents, max-cents
        (and does NOT compute mean — mean is not a monoid)

    @accumulators
        finalised where mean-cents = sum-cents / count
        emitted ordered by key ascending
]

Running state is separate from output state: monoids (sum/min/max)
combine pairwise during observation; non-monoids (mean) derive only
at finalise. This is what makes the whole thing one pass.

## Distinctive Innate idiom: malformed lines skipped `where` fields incomplete

[ta[parse {text: @text}]
    lines of @text
        where line is blank or begins with "#" -> skip
        where fields count is less than 3        -> skip
        where date or category is empty          -> skip
        where amount is not an integer           -> skip
        otherwise                                 -> parse into Transaction
]

Silent acceptance of garbage produces zeros-that-look-like-real-data,
which is worse than a dropped row. Explicit `where` clauses surface
the policy the resolver applies.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @sample <- "2026-01-03,groceries,4500\n" +
               "2026-01-10,groceries,3200\n" +
               "2026-01-12,rent,120000\n" +
               "2026-02-01,rent,120000\n" +
               "2026-02-14,groceries,5500\n" +
               "2026-02-22,books,2200\n"

    @txns <- [ta[parse {text: @sample}]]

    -> [ta[by-category {txns: @txns}]]
    ;; -> [("books",     count=1 mean=2200)
    ;;     ("groceries", count=3 mean=4400)
    ;;     ("rent",      count=2 mean=120000)]

    -> [ta[top-n-by-mean
             {groups: [ta[by-category {txns: @txns}]], n: 2}]]
    ;; -> [("rent", 120000), ("groceries", 4400)]
]
